From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] image: the guide image at the size of the hires pass

A run with a guide image (ControlNet) and the hires fix ended the process:
the hires pass gave the ControlNet the guide at the first pass's size, which
does not match the larger hires latent, and ggml asserted
(ggml_can_repeat(b, a), ggml.c), which aborts. On the PS5 that ended the
title: SDXL with xinsir's Canny ControlNet, 1024x1024 and a hires scale of
1.5.

The hires pass now gets the guide scaled to its own size (bilinear, clamped
to 0..1), as the mask of an inpainting run already is. Checked with the same
ControlNet on the CPU: 256x256 with a scale of 1.5 ran to its end.
---
 src/pipeline/image.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/pipeline/image.cpp b/src/pipeline/image.cpp
index 5e7a349..fac78c1 100644
--- a/src/pipeline/image.cpp
+++ b/src/pipeline/image.cpp
@@ -1118,6 +1118,17 @@ namespace sd::pipeline {
                 } else {
                     hires_control_image = latents.control_image;
                 }
+            } else if (!latents.control_image.empty()) {
+                // PS5SD: the guide image (ControlNet) at the size of the hires pass. The first pass's
+                // does not match the hires latent, and ggml asserts on it (ggml_can_repeat), which
+                // ends the process.
+                hires_control_image = sd::ops::interpolate(latents.control_image,
+                                                           {request.hires.target_width,
+                                                            request.hires.target_height,
+                                                            latents.control_image.shape()[2],
+                                                            latents.control_image.shape()[3]},
+                                                           sd::ops::InterpolateMode::Bilinear);
+                hires_control_image = sd::ops::clamp(hires_control_image, 0.0f, 1.0f);
             }
             for (int b = 0; b < (int)final_latents.size(); b++) {
                 if (sd->get_cancel_flag() == SD_CANCEL_ALL) {
